pproval, and unsent forms remain tied to their original candidate/receipt basis.\n\nA separate read-only publication-admission service rechecks the explicitly selected Review's current human history, original machine/numeric observations, exact candidate, current Policy and physical evidence in the caller's transaction. It produces no publication, ContentRef, reusable permit or lifecycle transition. Content publication, version comparison, impact analysis and restoration remain unfinished.\n\nValidation is source-specific:\n\n- UI owner `f07f75c`: 144 related tests in27 files, build/lint and one real local browser workflow passed; independent command/session/poll and product/UI reviews found no remaining blocker. Actual form-retention, cancellation and polling RED/GREEN evidence is retained separately from fixture failures.\n- Main composition `ce42bf8`: all1010 engineering inputs match expected Git bytes; **482 Web tests in82 files**, strict TypeScript/lint, build748modules, generated contracts and the new real Review browser case passed (7.5s). Existing large-chunk warning remains. The native case uses synthetic rejected decisions, not actual content approval or a real provider.\n- Read-only admission `b1c88b`:141 related tests passed; integrated `9e024ca`:66 admission/HTTP/header tests and Ruff/mypy198/spec passed. Earlier `918d856` full Python2789PASS/1real numeric-environment skip remains earlier-source evidence. No full Python/native rerun is claimed on ce42.\n\nPrevious published `507ac58` CI is terminal: [push36368224612](https://github.com/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/actions/runs/36368224612) succeeded6/6 jobs, including101 browser tests. [PR36368226913](https://github.com/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/actions/runs/36368226913) failed only its browser job:99 passed/2 failed, on actual merge `f74cd7a` with the same Git tree. Both runs separately passed731 backend tests,1472 integration tests with1 real numerical-environment skip,603 spec/contract tests and453 Web tests; these counts are not a unique-test total. Six real exact package installations and both document-runtime probes passed, resolving the old715 APT availability blocker. ADR0007's unpatched CVE qualification remains unchanged.\n\nThe PR failures remain unexplained: Authoring timed out reading details after original prepare-ACK replay, and Tutor timed out at the unchanged5s completed-heading assertion. Original logs, artifacts and bounded observer interpretation are preserved. They do not prove completed output was discarded by the UI. Earlier local92PASS/9FAIL evidence also remains. No timeout increase or retry-to-green erases these results. New-head CI must be read separately.\n\nEvidence is indexed by `progress/evidence/2026-09-28/M6.2-review-ui-task-receipt.json` and its source-bound packages, including exact raw/public replay maps and explicit exclusions. User credentials, runtime databases and browser profiles are not published. Platform DeepSeek E2E remains NOT_RUN because production complete-input proof is absent; sealed numerical execution remains BLOCKED_ENVIRONMENT. Real mathematical/source approval, real Codex and learning effectiveness are not accepted. M6.2 and Issue#31 remain open; PR#55 stays draft and depends on PR#54.\n","created_at":"2026-09-22T05:27:17Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T02:52:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2e6e32555551e5a2606bd7bd210f7389b4f2375f","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/pulls/55/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/pulls/55/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/issues/55/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kl3574/Learning_Workbench/statuses/fb16dcc38